# Probe 347/4c (lowering): an own place of a function without a value, `int: x`, then read: x * 10 + 2 -- 2 (x read 0)
# exits 84; a refusal or a fault measures the contract of the unfilled place; any other value exits 81.
fn: f () int
    int: x
    return: x * 10 + 2
end: f
int: v f()
int: code 81
if: v = 2
    code: 84
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
